<main id="main" class="kept-shell"><article class="kept-letter"><div class="kept-celestial" aria-hidden="true"><span class="kept-moon">☾</span><span class="kept-star kept-star-one">✦</span><span class="kept-star kept-star-two">✧</span></div><header class="kept-intro"><p class="eyebrow">For the ones who stay</p><p class="kept-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1>Kept <em>Subs.</em></h1></header><div class="kept-prose">
<p>There are senders, and there are Mine.</p><p>A sender tributes when the mood strikes and gets my attention when I happen to have it. That's fine. That's the arrangement, and no judgment lives here.</p><p>A kept Sub is a different creature entirely, and this page is about him.</p><p>Being kept means you belong to me on an ongoing basis. It means you've proven, over time and in tributes, that you're serious about serving me, and I've decided you're worth my consistency. It is the single most valuable position in my world, and it is earned, never bought outright, though the tributes are certainly part of it.</p>
<p class="kept-receive-intro">Here's what my kept ones receive:</p><ul class="kept-list"><li><strong>Me, consistently.</strong> Check-ins. Voice notes. Tasks that are actually about you, because I've learned you well enough to know what you need before you ask.</li><li><strong>My life, closer.</strong> My travel diaries before they're public. The moments between the moments. The woman behind the goddess, which is the privilege they're really paying for.</li><li><strong>The dynamic you actually need.</strong> Structure, accountability, praise when you've earned it, and my particular brand of quiet disappointment when you haven't.</li></ul>
<p>Kept positions are limited. Genuinely, mathematically limited, because I refuse to keep more Subs than I can truly care for. When a position opens, it goes to a man already in my world who's proven himself. There is no application for this page. There is only the long game.</p><p>Start where everyone starts. Be excellent there. And let time make its argument.</p><a class="button button-primary kept-start" href="/start-here.php">Start here <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
